wine-sg (10.0-239) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Credential Manager keeps credentials in the person's keyring (patch
    1380). CredWrite kept every saved credential in the user's registry
    hive, only RC4-scrambled with a key stored beside it. Credentials kept
    beyond the logon session now go to the keyring of the Unix account the
    program runs as (gnome-keyring's Secret Service on the session bus,
    through libsecret loaded by a new Unix side of advapi32, advapi32.so),
    encrypted with the sign-in password; CredRead, CredEnumerate and
    CredDelete find them there, target names matching without regard to
    case. What the registry holds moves there at the next use with a
    keyring; the registry stays the fallback, with a warning, with no
    session bus (SYSTEM's services) or a locked keyring (never a prompt),
    and keeps logon-session credentials. Real Git Credential Manager (Git
    for Windows 2.47.1) stores, gets and erases through it; sg-shell's
    Remote Desktop "Remember me" and Credential Manager page use it. Gate
    test-credkeyring (test/credkeyring-gate.sh, 64- and 32-bit probe),
    mutants SG_MUTANT_CRED_KEYRING and SG_MUTANT_CRED_MIGRATE.

